  "privacy": {
    "meta": {
      "title": "Privacy Policy · DropFlow",
      "description": "Your files stay on your device. No uploads, no accounts, no cookies, no tracking. Open source, so anyone can check."
    },
    "title": "Privacy Policy",
    "lead": "Short version: your files stay on your device, and we collect nothing about you.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "h": "Your files",
        "ul": [
          "They are converted on your device: in the Windows app, or inside this browser tab.",
          "They are never uploaded, to us or to anyone else.",
          "In the browser they stay in memory only and are gone when you close the tab."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "What we collect",
        "ul": [
          "Nothing. No accounts, no ads, no analytics, no tracking.",
          "This website sets no cookies and loads no third-party scripts."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "When the internet is used",
        "ul": [
          "To open this website, and when the Windows app checks GitHub for updates.",
          "When you give the web app a link: your browser downloads that one file straight from that site (a plain download, no cookies). Nothing is uploaded.",
          "Optional AI models and helper programs in the Windows app, only after you agree.",
          "Send to phone: a temporary server on your own Wi-Fi, only while its window is open."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Stored on your device",
        "ul": [
          "Web app: an offline copy of the app and one setting (the large-file warning). Clear the site data in your browser to remove it.",
          "Windows app: settings, a list of recent conversions (names and paths, never contents), logs and models, in %LocalAppData%\\DropFlow. Delete that folder to remove them."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Other services",
        "p": [
          "Vercel hosts this website, GitHub hosts the downloads and updates, and Hugging Face hosts the optional AI models. Like any server they keep normal request logs (such as your IP address), under their own privacy policies."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Check it yourself",
        "p": [
          "DropFlow is open source (GPL-3.0). The source code is public, so anyone can check every line of this page."
        ],
        "links": [
          "source"
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Who we are",
        "p": [
          "Developed by the ScoutHub teams. Lead developer: Moustafa Al-Hamwi, Lebanon."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Changes",
        "p": [
          "If anything here changes, we update this page and its date."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "terms": {
    "meta": {
      "title": "Terms of Use · DropFlow",
      "description": "DropFlow is free software under the GPL-3.0-or-later: use it, change it and share it. No warranty."
    },
    "title": "Terms of Use",
    "lead": "DropFlow is free software. Use it, change it and share it, under the GPL-3.0.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "h": "The licence",
        "p": [
          "DropFlow is free and open-source software under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later). The GPL is the binding text; this page only explains it in plain words."
        ],
        "links": [
          "gpl",
          "license",
          "source"
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "You may",
        "ul": [
          "Use it for anything, at home or at work, for free.",
          "Read the code and change it.",
          "Share copies, changed or not, even for money, as long as you keep the GPL: same licence, notices kept, full source code available.",
          "Keep what you make: the GPL covers the software, not the files you convert."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Name and logo",
        "p": [
          "The GPL covers the code, not the name \"DropFlow\" or its logo. A changed version you publish needs its own name and logo."
        ],
        "links": [
          "trademark"
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Your files",
        "ul": [
          "You need the right to use the files you convert, and the right to download any link you give the app.",
          "DropFlow never overwrites your originals: results are new files. Still, check them and keep backups."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Know the limits",
        "ul": [
          "PDF sign adds a visible stamp. It is not a legal or cryptographic digital signature.",
          "PDF redact only finds words in the text layer. Mark scanned pages yourself, and check the result before you share it.",
          "PDF crop only hides content; it is still inside the file. Use redact to remove it.",
          "AI results (speech to text, OCR, background removal) can be wrong. Check them."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "No warranty",
        "p": [
          "DropFlow comes \"as is\", with no warranty of any kind, as far as the law allows (GPL-3.0, section 15). You use it at your own risk."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Liability",
        "p": [
          "As far as the law allows, nobody who writes or shares DropFlow is liable for damage from using it, including lost data (GPL-3.0, sections 16 and 17)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Third-party parts",
        "p": [
          "Some included components have their own licences. They are listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES."
        ],
        "links": [
          "notices"
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Changes",
        "p": [
          "We may update this page; the date above shows the latest version. An update never takes away GPL rights you already have."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Who we are",
        "p": [
          "Developed by the ScoutHub teams. Lead developer: Moustafa Al-Hamwi, Lebanon."
        ]
